" Useful tidbits
"
" Substitution operation for replacing "P<T> arg" method declarations with
" "P<T> const& arg".  Explanation:
"
" \1 = P<T> + spaces
" \2 = (const& + spaces) not present
" \3 = argument name + \4
" \4 = , 
"    or )
"    or spaces + '//' to end of line
"    or spaces to end of line
"    or end of line
" (Obviously, \4 could be simplified or optimized)
" This pattern should also ignore a leading '//'
" :s/\(\<P<\w*>\s*\)\(const\s*&\s*\)\{0}\(\<\w*\>\([,)]\|\s*\/\/.*$\|\s\s*$\|$\)\)/\1const\& \3/g
"
" The equivalent Perl regular expression, for use with 'grep -P' is
"       \bP<\w*>\s*(const\s*&\s*){0}\b\w*\b([,)]|\s*\/\/.*$|\s\s*$|$)

